- # `↯/s.106.3` — `Json.Provider.Error`
+ # `↯/s.106.3` — `Json.Provider.Error`

- Raised when a JSON value does not satisfy the schema it is being
- validated against.
+ Levée lorsqu'une valeur JSON ne satisfait pas le schéma par rapport auquel elle
+ est validée.

- ## Cause
+ ## Cause

- Jacinta's `Json.Provider` validates JSON values against a schema as a record's fields are read,
- and reports each mismatch via this error, through the `Tactic` of the code reading the field, so
- that a validating reader can collect them all. The message is `the
+ Le `Json.Provider` de Jacinta valide des valeurs JSON par rapport à un schéma à mesure que les
+ champs d'un enregistrement sont lus, et signale chaque non-conformité par cette erreur, au moyen
+ du `Tactic` du code qui lit le champ, afin qu'un lecteur validant puisse toutes les recueillir.
+ Le message est `the

- JSON was not valid according to the schema because $reason`.
+ JSON was not valid according to the schema because $reason`.

- ## Variants
+ ## Variantes

- ```tabular
+ ```tabular

- column  Code
+ column  Code

- column  Reason
- column  Meaning
+ column  Raison
+ column  Signification

- column  Message
+ column  Message

- column  Resolution
- row  `↯/s.106.3.1`  `JsonType`  The value's type does not match what the schema requires.  `[↯/s.106.3.1] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because expected JSON type number, but found string`  Provide a value of the type the schema requires, or relax the schema if the type is genuinely flexible.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.2`  `MissingValue`  A required value is absent from the JSON. The reason names the missing field where it is known.  `[↯/s.106.3.2] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value of locality was missing`  Add the missing field, or mark it optional in the schema.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.3`  `IntOutOfRange`  An integer value falls outside the `minimum`/`maximum` allowed by the schema. Raised by the `"integer!"` provider type; an absent bound is `Unset` rather than a sentinel.  `[↯/s.106.3.3] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value was not between 1 and 99`  Constrain the value to the schema's permitted range.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.4`  `PatternMismatch`  A string value does not match the regular expression in the schema's `pattern`.  `[↯/s.106.3.4] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value did not conform to the regular expression [a-z]+`  Adjust the value to match the schema's pattern, or loosen the pattern.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.5`  `NumberOutOfRange`  A number falls outside the `minimum`/`maximum` (or exclusive bounds) the schema declares. Raised by the `"number!"` provider type.  `[↯/s.106.3.5] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the number was not between -90.0 and 90.0`  Constrain the value to the schema's permitted range.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.6`  `LengthOutOfRange`  A string's length falls outside the schema's `minLength`/`maxLength`. Raised by the `"string!"` provider type.  `[↯/s.106.3.6] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the string's length was not between 1 and 214`  Shorten or lengthen the value to fit the schema.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.7`  `NotPermitted`  A string is not one of the schema's `enum` values (or its `const`). Raised by the `"enum"` provider type.  `[↯/s.106.3.7] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value Polygon was not one of Point`  Use one of the listed values, or extend the schema's `enum`.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.8`  `UnexpectedKind`  A value is of a JSON kind which none of the alternatives of its union (`anyOf`, `oneOf`, or a `type` naming several) accepts.  `[↯/s.106.3.8] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value was a JSON boolean, which is not one of string, number`  Give a value of one of the kinds the schema lists.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.9`  `Unparsable`  A string's text is not valid for its `format`: a `json-pointer` or a `regex` which does not parse.  `[↯/s.106.3.9] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value a[ is not a valid regex`  Correct the value so that it parses in its format.
+ column  Résolution
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.1`  `JsonType`  Le type de la valeur ne correspond pas à ce qu'exige le schéma.  `[↯/s.106.3.1] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because expected JSON type number, but found string`  Fournissez une valeur du type qu'exige le schéma, ou assouplissez le schéma si le type est réellement variable.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.2`  `MissingValue`  Une valeur obligatoire est absente du JSON. La raison nomme le champ manquant lorsqu'il est connu.  `[↯/s.106.3.2] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value of locality was missing`  Ajoutez le champ manquant, ou marquez-le comme optionnel dans le schéma.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.3`  `IntOutOfRange`  Une valeur entière se situe hors des bornes `minimum`/`maximum` qu'autorise le schéma. Levée par le type de fournisseur `"integer!"` ; une borne absente vaut `Unset` plutôt qu'une valeur sentinelle.  `[↯/s.106.3.3] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value was not between 1 and 99`  Limitez la valeur à l'intervalle autorisé par le schéma.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.4`  `PatternMismatch`  Une valeur chaîne ne correspond pas à l'expression régulière du `pattern` du schéma.  `[↯/s.106.3.4] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value did not conform to the regular expression [a-z]+`  Adaptez la valeur au motif du schéma, ou assouplissez le motif.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.5`  `NumberOutOfRange`  Un nombre se situe hors des bornes `minimum`/`maximum` (ou des bornes exclusives) que déclare le schéma. Levée par le type de fournisseur `"number!"`.  `[↯/s.106.3.5] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the number was not between -90.0 and 90.0`  Limitez la valeur à l'intervalle autorisé par le schéma.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.6`  `LengthOutOfRange`  La longueur d'une chaîne se situe hors des bornes `minLength`/`maxLength` du schéma. Levée par le type de fournisseur `"string!"`.  `[↯/s.106.3.6] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the string's length was not between 1 and 214`  Raccourcissez ou allongez la valeur pour qu'elle respecte le schéma.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.7`  `NotPermitted`  Une chaîne ne fait pas partie des valeurs `enum` du schéma (ni de sa `const`). Levée par le type de fournisseur `"enum"`.  `[↯/s.106.3.7] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value Polygon was not one of Point`  Utilisez l'une des valeurs listées, ou étendez l'`enum` du schéma.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.8`  `UnexpectedKind`  Une valeur est d'une sorte JSON qu'aucune des alternatives de son union (`anyOf`, `oneOf`, ou un `type` qui en nomme plusieurs) n'accepte.  `[↯/s.106.3.8] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value was a JSON boolean, which is not one of string, number`  Donnez une valeur de l'une des sortes que liste le schéma.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.9`  `Unparsable`  Le texte d'une chaîne n'est pas valide pour son `format` : un `json-pointer` ou une `regex` qui ne s'analyse pas.  `[↯/s.106.3.9] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value a[ is not a valid regex`  Corrigez la valeur pour qu'elle s'analyse dans son format.

